<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip de Montmorency, Count of Horn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1524">1524</a>–<a href="/years/1568">1568</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Count of Hoorn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip de Montmorency (1524–1568), Count of Horne, was a nobleman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, admiral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and a knight of the Golden Fleece. With Egmont and William of Orange he led the noble opposition to Philip II's religious policy. Arrested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-alvarez-de-toledo-3rd-duke-of-alba">Duke of Alba</a> in 1567, he was beheaded with Egmont on the Grand Place in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> on 5 June 1568.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-de-montmorency-count-of-horn.jpg" alt="Philip de Montmorency, Count of Horn" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gysius-Oorsprong-en-voortgang_9090.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
